`src/what/difficulty.ts` and `src/what/parameters.ts` are copied verbatim from
the Proof of What? node software and are not maintained here. They are the same
code the Stratum server runs, ported from `lib/what/difficulty.ak` and
`lib/what/parameters.ak` in:

  - proofofwhat/contracts (https://github.com/proofofwhat/contracts), Apache-2.0

Not file for file: a few constants in `parameters.ts` live elsewhere in that
repository or nowhere in it, and each says so where it is defined.

`test/parity-vectors.json` is generated from `lib/what/parity.ak` in the same
repository, and records the revision it was taken from. `npm run parity` runs
it against the vendored rule.

The validator in that repository is where the difficulty rule is specified and
enforced. Everything else in this repository models a chain around it.

`README.md` is documentation rather than code and carries the same licence as
the rest of this repository.
